the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base termlife_issue includes these resources:
    temporal.

the functions are:
    the face amount of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the billing mode of *an activity* is *a value*.
    the effective date of *an activity* is *a date*.
    the insured date of birth of the policy before *an activity* is *a date*.
    the insured gender of the policy before *an activity* is *a value*.
    the insured tobacco of the policy before *an activity* is *a value*.
    the issue age of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the premium rate of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the annual premium of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the modal factor of *an activity* is *a number*.
    the modal premium of *an activity* is *an amount*.
    the policy fee of the plan is *an amount*.
    the issue date of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.
    the paid to date of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.
    the face amount of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.
    the billing mode of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.
    the modal premium of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.
    the policy status of the policy after *an activity* is *a value*.

the templates are:
    *an activity* is an issue.
    *an activity* fails the check *a code*.
    the term premium rate for issue age *a issue age* and gender *a gender* and tobacco *a tobacco* is *a rate* under table term_premium.

the table term_premium is loaded from term_premium.csv, with unique match:
    issue age | gender | tobacco | rate

the knowledge base termlife_issue includes:

the text of "Issue/Transaction.xml" is at "sources/Issue/Transaction.xml".

the policy fee of the plan is 60, as stated in "PlanFields.csv" at PolicyFee.

% An activity of this program is an issue: the Issue transaction it processes.
an activity is an issue if
    the effective date of the activity is a date.

rule issue_age with provenance "Issue/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable IssueAgeMV:
the issue age of an activity is a number if
    a date is 6 months after the effective date of the activity
    and the age on the date of someone born on the insured date of birth of the policy before the activity is the number.

rule premium_rate with provenance "Issue/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable PremiumRateMV:
the premium rate of an activity is a number N if
    the issue age of the activity is a second number
    and the insured gender of the policy before the activity is a value
    and the insured tobacco of the policy before the activity is a second value
    and the term premium rate for issue age the second number and gender the value and tobacco the second value is N under table term_premium
    otherwise the activity is an issue
    and N = 0.

rule annual_premium with provenance "Issue/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable AnnualPremiumMV:
the annual premium of an activity is an amount N if
    the face amount of the activity is an amount M
    and the premium rate of the activity is a number K
    and the policy fee of the plan is an amount P
    and N = round((M / 1000 * K + P) * 100) / 100.

rule modal_factor with provenance "Issue/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable ModalFactorMV:
the modal factor of an activity is a number N if
    the billing mode of the activity is a value
    and the value is equal to "12"
    and N = 0.0875
    otherwise the billing mode of the activity is a second value
    and the second value is equal to "04"
    and N = 0.26
    otherwise the billing mode of the activity is a third value
    and the third value is equal to "02"
    and N = 0.51
    otherwise the activity is an issue
    and N = 1.

rule modal_premium with provenance "Issue/Transaction.xml" at MathVariable ModalPremiumMV:
the modal premium of an activity is an amount N if
    the annual premium of the activity is an amount M
    and the modal factor of the activity is a number K
    and N = round(M * K * 100) / 100.

% The insured's issue age of [the issue age] is outside 18 to 65.
rule i001 with provenance "Issue/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression I001:
an activity fails the check "I001" if
    the issue age of the activity is a number N
    and N < 18
        or N > 65.

% The face amount must be at least $50,000.
rule i002 with provenance "Issue/ValidateExpressions.xml" at Expression I002:
an activity fails the check "I002" if
    the face amount of the activity < 50000.

rule copy_issue_date with provenance "Issue/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field IssueDate:
the issue date of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the effective date of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

rule copy_paid_to_date with provenance "Issue/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field PaidToDate:
the paid to date of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the effective date of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

rule copy_face_amount with provenance "Issue/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field FaceAmount:
the face amount of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the face amount of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

rule copy_billing_mode with provenance "Issue/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field BillingMode:
the billing mode of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the billing mode of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

rule copy_modal_premium with provenance "Issue/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field ModalPremium:
the modal premium of the policy after an activity is a value if
    the modal premium of the activity is the value
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

rule copy_policy_status with provenance "Issue/CopyToPolicyFields.xml" at Field PolicyStatus:
the policy status of the policy after an activity is Active if
    the activity is an issue
    and it is not the case that the activity fails the check a code.

